- "prereq": the ONE concept the reader most likely needed first for the original to make sense. "concept" is a short name, "why" is one sentence on what it unlocks. If the original needed no prerequisite and was just badly written, set prereq to null.

HARD CONSTRAINT: the claim, its confidence rating, and its evidential basis do not change. You are making it easier to grasp, never easier to believe. Do not add certainty, do not drop caveats, do not upgrade a speculative claim. If the original was folklore or contested, the plainer version must be just as clearly folklore or contested.`;
  return parse(await callClaude(sys,
    `Topic: ${card.topic}\nClaim: ${card.idea}\nRating: ${card.tier}\nBasis: ${card.basis}\nOriginal: ${card.body}`,1000));
}

async function adjudicate(card,note){
  const sys=`You are refereeing a disagreement about how a scientific claim was rated. Return ONLY JSON, no fences:
{"concede","hold","settles_it","revised_tier"}
- "concede": what is genuinely right in the objection, specifically. If nothing is, say so.
- "hold": what still does not follow, with the number, scale, or theorem that does the work.
- "settles_it": the observation, measurement, or calculation that would decide it either way.
- "revised_tier": one of established/frontier/contested/folklore after weighing the objection. Change it only if warranted.
Be direct. Do not flatter and do not cave to persistence. Getting this right matters more than agreement.

${ACCURACY}`;
  return parse(await callClaude(sys,
    `Claim: "${card.idea}"\nRated: ${card.tier}\nStated basis: ${card.basis}\n\nObjection:\n${note}`,1200));
}

function renderCard(){
  const c=cards[idx],t=TIERS[c.tier]||TIERS.contested;
  const existing=threads.find(x=>x.card.idea===c.idea);
  const isRev=!!c._revisit,isRetake=!!c._retake;
  cardStart=Date.now();
  if(!isRetake){touched=false;retakeDone=false;}
  $('pips').innerHTML=cards.map((_,i)=>`<div class="pip ${cards[i]._revisit?'rev':''} ${i<=idx?'done':''}"></div>`).join('');
  const lk=c.link&&c.link.strength;
  const yt=c.watch?`https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=${encodeURIComponent(c.watch)}`:'';
  $('stage').innerHTML=`
    <article class="card ${isRev?'revisit':''} ${isRetake?'retake':''}">
      ${isRetake?`<div class="retake-note">Second pass, level ${lvl(c.topic)}</div>`:''}
      <div class="topic"><span class="eyebrow" ${isRev?'style="color:var(--revisit)"':''}>${isRev?'Revisit / ':''}${esc(c.topic)}</span><span class="eyebrow">L${lvl(c.topic)}</span></div>
      ${c.hook?`<p class="body" style="font-style:italic;margin-bottom:14px">${esc(c.hook)}</p>`:''}
      <h2 class="idea">${esc(c.idea)}</h2>
      <p class="body">${esc(c.body)}</p>
      <div class="meter">
        <div class="meter-head"><span class="tier" style="color:${t.c}">${t.label}</span><span class="eyebrow">Confidence</span></div>
        <div class="bar"><div class="fill" id="fill" style="background:${t.c}"></div></div>
        <p class="basis">${esc(c.basis)}</p>
        ${existing&&existing.note?`<div class="flagged"><span class="eyebrow">Your objection</span>${esc(existing.note)}</div>`:''}
      </div>
      ${yt?`<a class="watch" id="ytl" href="${esc(yt)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch &nbsp;<b>${esc(c.watch)}</b></a>`:''}
      ${lk?`<div class="linkbox"><h4>Tie to the bench</h4><p><span class="linkto">${esc(c.link.to)}</span></p>
        <p><span class="strength" style="color:${LINKCOLOR[c.link.strength]||'var(--muted)'}">${esc(c.link.strength)}</span></p>
        <p>${esc(c.link.mechanism)}</p></div>`:''}
      ${c.tier==='frontier'&&c.open_question?`<details class="work" id="det"><summary>Open the problem</summary>
        <h4>The open question</h4><p>${esc(c.open_question)}</p>
        <h4>Where it stalls</h4><p>${esc(c.stuck_on)}</p>
        <h4>Handles</h4><ul class="handles">${(c.handles||[]).map(h=>`<li>${esc(h)}</li>`).join('')}</ul></details>`:''}
      <div id="verdict"></div>
      <div class="dispute" id="disp" hidden>
        <textarea id="note" placeholder="What's wrong with this rating, and what's your evidence?">${existing?esc(existing.note):''}</textarea>
        <button class="btn small ghost" id="save-note" style="margin-top:8px">Record and referee</button>
      </div>
    </article>
    <div class="rowbtns">
      <button class="btn small ghost" id="overhead">Over my head</button>
      ${isRev?`<button class="btn small ghost" id="resolve">Settled</button>
               <button class="btn small ghost" id="challenge">Add objection</button>`
             :`<button class="btn small ghost" id="challenge">Dispute</button>
               <button class="btn small ${existing?'ghost':''}" id="benchit">${existing?'Benched':'Work on this'}</button>`}
      <button class="btn small" id="nxt">${idx===cards.length-1?'Finish':'Next'}</button>
    </div>`;
  requestAnimationFrame(()=>{const f=$('fill');if(f)f.style.width=t.w;});
